From 75ae28c854dc8863c4bfd47194a30037d8ce881a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: R0ck <random@email.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 02:02:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kiss_modem): runtime LoRa sync word and preamble
 overrides

Add KISS SetHardware sub-commands so a host can drive non-MeshCore LoRa
networks (e.g. Meshtastic, sync word 0x2B):

  0x1B SetSyncWord  sync(1)            -> OK / Error
  0x1C SetPreamble  symbols(u16 LE)    -> OK / Error (0 = default, else 6..65535)
  0x1D GetPhyExtra                     -> 0x9D sync(1) + preamble(u16 LE)

KISS_FIRMWARE_VERSION is bumped to 2 so hosts can detect support.

RadioLibWrapper gains setLoRaSyncWord() (dispatching to each chip's RadioLib
setSyncWord) and setPreambleOverride(). The preamble override survives
setParams()/updatePreamble(), is used for the header/payload RX timeouts and
the LR11x0/LR2021 post-TX preamble reset, and both overrides are re-applied
after AGC resets. Defaults are unchanged when the commands are not used.

Also only call Serial.setTxTimeoutMs() when Serial is HWCDC
(ARDUINO_USB_CDC_ON_BOOT), fixing the Heltec_v3_kiss_modem build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014ezDJkF9APrttJ1fHwhsVA
